 its close encounter and in the following days, this inspired composited scene covers the dim outer planet, largest moon Triton, and faint system of rings. From just beyond Neptune's orbit, the interplanetary perspective looks back toward the Sun, capturing the planet and Triton as thin sunlit crescents. Cirrus clouds and a dark band circle Neptune's south polar region, with a cloudy vortex above the pole itself. Parts of the very faint ring system along with the three bright ring arcs were first imaged by Voyager during the fly-by, though the faintest segments are modeled in this composited picture. Spanning 7.5 degrees, the background starfield is composed from sky survey data centered on the constellation Camelopardalis, corresponding to the outbound Voyager's view of the magnificent Neptunian system. Still cruising in 2026, the Voyager 2 spacecraft is now in interstellar space.","img":"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Neptune-South-Pole-Voyager-2_2327x1670.jpg?w=1400&fit=clip","by":"Assembly/Processing - Rolf Olsen, Data - Voyager 2, NASA Planetary Data System","video":false},"tle":["1 25544U 98067A   26324.88180268  .00009897  00000+0  18414-3 0  9991","2 25544  51.6319 244.6605 0007389  48.0812 312.0806 15.49518511596048"],"passes":[{"start":"2026-11-21T17:36:05Z","end":"2026-11-21T17:40:40Z","top":"2026-11-21T17:39:26Z","max":89,"from":["W","西"],"to":["E","東"],"mins":5},{"start":"2026-11-21T19:12:52Z","end":"2026-11-21T19:13:34Z","top":"2026-11-21T19:16:12Z","max":68,"from":["W","西"],"to":["W","西"],"mins":1},{"start":"2026-11-22T16:48:08Z","end":"2026-11-22T16:54:49Z","top":"2026-11-22T16:51:28Z","max":84,"from":["W","西"],"to":["E","東"],"mins":7},{"start":"2026-11-22T18:24:55Z","end":"2026-11-22T18:27:44Z","top":"2026-11-22T18:28:16Z","max":81,"from":["W","西"],"to":["W","西"],"mins":3},{"start":"2026-11-23T17:36:56Z","end":"2026-11-23T17:41:32Z","top":"2026-11-23T17:40:17Z","max":90,"from":["W","西"],"to":[